MEMORY_UPDATE/v1

2026-09-11 P(-1) integration produced a new canonical blocker fixture: #121 `FRIDAY-RELEASE-COMMANDER-0001` was intended as a deadline-bound authority role but existing mailbox semantics reduced it to a one-shot TaskLease. Observed durable sequence: CLAIMED -> EXECUTION_FINISHED(exit=0, ~50s) -> TASK_BLOCKED, artifact_count=0. Semantic objective (persistent release control loop through 18:00) was not achieved.

Prometheus classification candidate:
- blocker_class: representation / authority-lifecycle mismatch;
- semantic_work_status: unknown/not-started for release objective;
- retry_safety: do not blindly replay the same mailbox representation;
- minimum_missing representation: `RoleLease` / `CommanderLease` distinct from `TaskLease`;
- next safe continuation: direct sovereign bootstrap for the time-boxed experiment, while retaining strict reporter semantics for subordinate tasks;
- Pasha required only for the bootstrap authority, not ordinary subordinate routing.

Invariant: `subprocess END != role DONE`. A RoleLease should survive subordinate task termination until deadline/revoke/budget exhaustion/sovereign boundary. It must not become a completion oracle.

#121 now contains the full `BUTTERFLY/v1` and cheapest two-subtask falsification test.
